  "notes": [
    "A Divisional Commander must select brigades from a single nationality (Saxon, Bavarian, Württemberg, Westphalian, Other Confederation States or Rheinbund).",
    "Württemberg: 1-2 Infantry Brigades (1-2 Line regiments), 0-1 Light Infantry Brigade (adds Jäger battalions), 0-1 Cavalry Brigade (1 per infantry brigade), Divisional Artillery.",
    "Bavaria: 1-3 Infantry Brigades (add Light Infantry battalion / Chevauleger regiment), 0-2 Cavalry Brigades (1 per infantry brigade, or if none attached), Divisional Artillery.",
    "Saxony: 1-2 Infantry Brigades (add Grenadier battalion), 0-1 Saxon Grenadier Brigade, up to 2 Light Cavalry Brigades (0-1 per infantry brigade), a Cavalry Reserve (Garde du Corps/Cuirassier/Polish Cuirassier).",
    "Westphalia: 0-1 Guard Infantry Brigade, 1-2 Infantry Brigades (max 7 battalions per brigade), 0-2 Cavalry Brigades, a Cavalry Reserve (Cuirassiers, if 2 infantry brigades taken), and an Artillery Reserve (1 Heavy Battery if 8 battalions taken).",
    "Other Confederation States: up to 1 Infantry Brigade per nationality (Baden, Hesse, Berg, etc.), 0-1 Cavalry Brigade (1 per infantry brigade).",
    "Rheinbund: up to 1 Infantry Brigade (1-3 regiments of 1-2 battalions); this brigade can be taken by any Divisional commander regardless of nationality.",
    "Allies: a Confederation of the Rhine army can take 25% allies from any one allied list."
  ]
